1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a048fc4569f5acf6894f34389985aca493fbf27e.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 16 at 4:11PM MDT until August 16 at 5:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"SVRPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nSoutheastern El Paso County in east central Colorado...\nNorthwestern Crowley County in southeastern Colorado...\nNortheastern Pueblo County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 500 PM MDT.\n\n* At 411 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Hanover, or\n23 miles northeast of Pueblo Airport, moving east at 10 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage\nto roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of\nsoutheastern El Paso, northwestern Crowley and northeastern Pueblo\nCounties.","ends":"2026-08-16T17:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Crowley, CO; El Paso, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4c68fd8da39688a6174e74d209b32e34b937d58.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a4c68fd8da39688a6174e74d209b32e34b937d58.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 16 at 4:02PM MDT until August 16 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 402 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain have ended across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of\nrain have fallen. Flooding impacts will continue, but no additional\nrainfall is expected. Flash flooding is expected to continue until\nthe water has a chance to recede.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nFountain, Fort Carson, Stratmoor and Security-Widefield.","ends":"2026-08-16T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"El Paso, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29fbb446cb1dc074d93b0bf3fd18e27407c81cce.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29fbb446cb1dc074d93b0bf3fd18e27407c81cce.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 16 at 3:53PM MDT until August 16 at 4:30PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 353 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Hanover, or 25\nmiles north of Pueblo Airport, moving east at 10 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and quarter size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Hail damage to vehicles is expected. Expect wind damage to\nroofs, siding, and trees.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nHanover.","ends":"2026-08-16T16:30:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"El Paso, CO; Pueblo, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.718d4ccd19ed7a97ac6852719fcbf3d0d764556c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.718d4ccd19ed7a97ac6852719fcbf3d0d764556c.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 16 at 2:44PM MDT until August 16 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n587 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 10 COUNTIES\n\nIN CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nTELLER\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nEL PASO\n\nIN SOUTHEAST COLORADO\n\nBACA                  BENT                  CROWLEY\nKIOWA                 LAS ANIMAS            OTERO\nPROWERS               PUEBLO\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF COLORADO SPRINGS, EADS, LA JUNTA,\nLAMAR, LAS ANIMAS, OLNEY SPRINGS, ORDWAY,\nPETERSON SPACE FORCE BASE, PUEBLO, ROCKY FORD, SPRINGFIELD,\nTRINIDAD, WALSH, AN